hexagon: htp: the weight stream of the HMX matmul on the DMA rings of the dequantization workers

The cost

From 5 rows the Q8_0 weight matmuls run on the pipelined HMX 2D loop. That loop moves each chunk of weight
tiles on the DMA ring of the op thread, as rows of one tile (1088 bytes) at the VTCM pitch 1152. In the
phone stage spf (the 4B Q8_0 on the v79 NPU, the depth 2300, the draft off), the weight matmuls use 62.3
to 66.7 ms of a call at 1 to 4 rows (the HVX matvec: six rings, one DMA row for each column tile) and 76.9
to 89.3 ms at 8 to 64 rows. At 22 rows one matmul of the attn_qkv shape uses 374 to 525 us against 357 to
382 us at 1 row, and the slow layers are the same in the two calls. The PMU counters at 8 and 22 rows (the
set dma-wait of tools/prof/pmu.py): the DMA is active 0.92 to 0.98 of the op, its read buffer is full 0.75
to 0.83 of the op (0.12 to 0.21 at 1 row), and the threads poll the DMA 0.35 to 0.45 of the op. The phase
trace at 22 rows: the dequantization uses 22 to 30 % of each op on each thread and the output 3 to 8 %, and
thread 0 waits for the DMA in the remaining time. Thus the weight stream sets the time of the op, and not
the conversion.

The change

The kernel param hmx_wstream (the slot of vtcm_src3_size, which no code read) selects the weight stream of
the pipelined loop for Q8_0 weights in hmx_mm_2d_f32 and hmx_mm_nx_2d_f32 (hmx_mm_q8_0_stream):
- 0, HTP_MM_WSTREAM_TILES: the loop as before.
- 1, HTP_MM_WSTREAM_PACKED: the op thread moves each chunk as one DMA row, thus the tiles are at the pitch
  of 1088 bytes in VTCM. dequantize_tiled_weight_to_fp16_task_q8_0_packed reads a tile with unaligned
  loads.
- 2, HTP_MM_WSTREAM_RINGS: the packed layout, and each dequantization worker moves its own tiles on its own
  ring. Worker w owns the tiles [w * per, (w + 1) * per) of each chunk, where per is its share of a full
  chunk. For a chunk it waits for its tiles on ctx->dma[w], dequantizes them, and then moves its tiles of
  the chunk two steps later into the same bytes. Only the last chunk can have fewer tiles, and a chunk two
  steps later exists only when the chunk is not the last, thus a worker writes only bytes of its own
  range. Worker w is thread w of the work queue, thus each ring stays on one thread.
The packed task reads two tiles from an even tile (17 vectors, 2176 bytes) with aligned loads, and puts the
vectors of the odd tile together with valign. A tile with no partner in its range goes alone.
The host gives the value of GGML_HEXAGON_MM_WSTREAM (the preset is 2, and a value outside 0 to 2 gives 0)
in the params of each HMX matmul of GGML_HEXAGON_MM_WSTREAM_ROWS rows or fewer (the preset is 32), and the
stream 0 to a larger matmul. The HMX jobs, the output transfers and their order do not change, and the
packed task does the arithmetic of the aligned task, thus the output has the bits of the stream 0.

The results

The kernel lab (tools/htp-lab, target mmchunks, the release flags with -flto, the functional mode with the
HMX, 1 MB of VTCM): MUL_MAT, MUL_MAT with src2 and MUL_MAT_NX with Q8_0 and F16 weights, 5 to 1000 rows,
k from 256 to 2560, the chunks of the two solvers and of requests (partial last chunks included). Each of
the 78 runs of the streams 1 and 2 gives the bytes of the stream 0, and no byte after dst changes (121
runs in 12 cases, 0 failures). The DMA shim of the lab copies at the push and the work queue of the lab
runs the workers one after the other, thus a worker that moves bytes into the range of a different worker
before that worker reads them changes the output.

The kernel lab, the Q8_0 dequantization task of one thread on 480 tiles in VTCM (target mmchunks with
--dq_tiles 480, the timing mode): 72.0 cycles for each tile with the aligned task and 74.0 cycles with the
packed task, and the same f16 bytes, also for ranges that start at an odd tile and end at an even tile. A packed task
with unaligned loads and loops that the compiler does not unroll keeps the 8 vectors of a tile on the
stack and uses 144.0 cycles.

The phone stage spf2 (the 4B Q8_0 on the v79 NPU, the library with the four candidates and the packed task
of 144 cycles, the stream on each HMX matmul, the depth 2300, the draft off). The wall time of a later call
(the median of 2 calls) and the W MM class of the op profile, the stream 2 against the stream 0 on the
same library:
    tokens  wall ms          W MM ms
    8       106.8 / 115.2    73.4 / 76.1
    22      115.3 / 122.3    73.0 / 77.7
    64      138.3 / 137.6    85.2 / 84.6
llama-bench pp512 was 3.4 % slower than HEAD in 3 paired rounds [-5.6, -2.1] and the logits prefill of 512
tokens took 520.4 ms against 510.1 ms with the stream 0: with many rows the HMX and the dequantization set
the time of the op, and the packed task used two times the cycles of the aligned task. The limit of 32
rows keeps pp512 and pp1024 on the stream 0. The logits hashes of a prompt of 512 tokens and 8 decode
tokens with the streams 0 and 2 are those of HEAD, and test-backend-ops of the Q8_0 MUL_MAT cases on HTP0
gives 43 of 43 passes.

